- $2.45B below in every column on the hold rows (-3.14 vs -0.69; -3.11 vs -0.66), and $2.56-2.57B below with the Re-engine.

That is 2045's $4.04B gap discounted five years (4.04 / 1.105^5 = 2.45): pure cost, no market gain.

Its item value is -2.10 to -2.14 on the hold rows. S3 on those rows is -3.14 and -3.11, past the -3.01 line, so Malave's buffer binds there. With the Re-engine, S3 is -2.95 and -2.93.

Embraer has been partnered with CFM since 2042. That gives CFM's engine a second airframe; it brings no airframe IP, capacity or strain relief that Boeing lacks. Via Embraer fails the partner test, so Solo.

