vetoes.ground:
Flag only, not a veto.

My safety, quality, ramp-shield, supply-crunch, engineering-capacity and absorption tests all pass, so there is no soft veto and no override is needed. The Board's condition on my results is met.

The flag is supply: no widebody engine is committed. UltraFan WB is ready in 2056 at best, against the board's 2055, and with no later round it may never reach the record.

I recommend hold on that flag and on the company's unmet $1B bar: the item is +0.58 at best and -0.41 in S6/S7. Of my tests, none stopped it. For the Board, hold rests on this flag and the doctrine bar.

If tabled, the flag is respected, and is not an unresolved objection, when the item carries:
- a public invitation for widebody engine proposals on standard terms;
- durability proven before entry into service;
- an EIS window that follows the engine, never 2055;
- the capacity step kept prepared.
With those I concur at veto check.

ops.would_change_mind_if:
